        <h1>Exercise Name: Standing Alternating Dumbbell Bicep Curl</h1>
        <u><h4><b>Exercise Overview</b></h4></u>
        
        This 3D anatomical visualization demonstrates Alternating Dumbbell Bicep Curls. The video highlights both bicep muscles (Biceps Brachii) in bright glowing colors, illustrating how alternating arms under strict control engages each bicep through flexion and supination (palms turning upward).

 Exercise Name: Standing Alternating Dumbbell Bicep Curl
 Target Muscles: Biceps (Biceps Brachii — short head and long head)
 Secondary Muscles: Brachialis, Brachioradialis (forearm flexors), Forearms
</div>
</div>
<pre>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1><u><h4><b>1.Setup: </b></h4></u>Stand up straight with feet shoulder-width apart, holding a dumbbell in each hand by your sides with your palms facing inward toward your thighs (neutral grip).
 <u><h4><b>2.Curling Phase: </b></h4></u>Keep your upper arms stationary and elbows tucked close to your torso. Exhale as you curl one dumbbell upward, rotating your wrist outward as you lift so that your palm faces up at the top position.
 <u><h4><b>3.Peak Squeeze: </b></h4></u>Pause for a split second at top shoulder height, firmly contracting your bicep.
 <u><h4><b>4.Lowering Phase: </b></h4></u>Inhale as you lower the dumbbell back down under control while rotating your wrist back to the neutral starting position. Repeat the movement with the opposite arm.

---

<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Unilateral Focus: </b>Concentrating on one arm at a time ensures equal effort and helps fix strength imbalances between left and right arms.
 <b>◉Optimal Supination: </b>Rotating your wrist outward during the curl maximizes contraction in both heads of the bicep.
 <b>◉Core & Grip Strength: </b>Standing execution engages your core for stability while building wrist and forearm grip strength.

---

<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 per arm | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Tone | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 per arm | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 4 – 5 | 6 – 8 per arm | 2 minutes |

Keep your torso still and avoid swinging your back or hips to move the dumbbells up
